#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186070018 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we wish to solve the compound inequality \n\n$$\n4 \\le x + 2 \\le 8.\n$$\n\nTo solve the compound inequality, we apply the usual operations to the middle of the inequality to isolate $x.$ Keep in mind that whatever we do to the middle, we also need to do to *both* the left-hand *and* right-hand sides.\n\nHere, we can isolate $x$ by subtracting $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t4 & \\le x + 2 \\le 8 \\[5pt]\n\t4 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} &\\le x + 2 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\le 8 \\,{\\color{red}-}\\, {\\color{red}{2}} \\[5pt]\n\t2 &\\le x \\le 6\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $2 \\le x \\le 6.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "6d8fae47-5e67-5793-a585-d3781d5c4555" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8677 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
